{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
  "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (U.S. Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General Clement: Mr. Chief Justice and may it please the Court: This case presents the same basic constitutional question concerning the Federal Partial-Birth Abortion Act as the first case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But the problem with this is that there -- well, some doctors absolutely agree. I mean, you know, my list over here, in which I have hundreds of references from this thing, is doctor after doctor who takes the other position, and they say:"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (U.S. Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Well, Justice Breyer, let me take as a point of departure the specific risks that you associated with the injection that induces fetal demise, because if there isn't a significant risk to that injection, then all the other benefits that are associated with the D&X procedure don't matter because they can perform the D&X procedure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I think you're wrong about -- you're probably wrong about this. But just before you leave, I mean, this is why it's so hard for me to get into the medical procedure. I heard you as saying, perhaps wrongly, that well, the doctor can always use a lethal injection to kill the fetus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (U.S. Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Justice Breyer, if I could respond to that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (U.S. Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0000-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Yes. And you can, you can, you can tell you can tell from the fact that a doctor, like one of the plaintiffs in the Nebraska case, Dr. Fitzhugh, says, that, well, I don't do the intact removal because if I wanted to do that I would have to do a second round of dilation with a second round of laminarias."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And therefore since the\nrisks were greater, the other side says that this\nactually shows it was safer. I mean, I don't know how\nto evaluate that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: I think it's even more\ncomplicated than that, Justice Breyer, because in fact,\nyou're right that the D&X patients were at a further\ngestational age, but the D&E patients were actually\nolder. And so I think --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsberg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBERG: Because your time is\nrunning out I did want to ask you about a feature of\nthis legislation that hasn't come up so far, and that is\nperhaps stimulated by Stenberg. But up until now, all\nregulation on access to abortion has been state\nregulation and this measure is saying to the states,\nlike it or not, the Federal Government is going to ban a\nparticular practice and we are going to take away the\nchoice from the states, in an area where up until now\nit's, it's been open to the states to make those\ndecisions. How should that weigh in this case? And it\nis something new."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Well, I mean I don't think\nit should figure in this Court's decision. I mean\nprincipally because the other side in neither case makes\na challenge based on the Commerce Clause, and I suppose\nthere is two reasons for that. That legal reason that\nthey don't bring the challenge is because there is a\njurisdictional element that I think would address the\nchallenges as a doctrinal matter. The practical reason\nI think is because this isn't the only instance in which\nthe Federal Government has gotten involved to address\nissues related to the abortion context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: General Clement, That\nbrings up a question I was intending to ask you. I\nnotice the finding says nothing about interstate\ncommerce but the statute says any physician who in or\naffecting interstate commerce performs the procedures.\nDoes that mean that the procedure is performed in a free\nclinic, as opposed to a profit organization, it would\nnot be covered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Miss Gartner, with regard\nto your argument that the statute here did not track\nwhat you have described as the characteristics, the\nhallmarks, I think the answer from the other side is\nthat the, the theory of this statute is a theory of a\nclear line between a legitimate abortion and\ninfanticide. And if that is the theory, then whether\nit's a breach delivery or a non-breach delivery is\nirrelevant. What would your answer be to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Ms. Gartner)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. GARTNER: Well, Your Honor, I think this gets to the point I was going to make about the safety of doing abortions in a way that would be banned by the law, and that's that in every D&E, regardless of whether the intent is to do an intact D&E or not an intact D&E, the intent is to minimize the insertion of instruments into the uterus and to extract the fetus as intact as possible, because each insertion of the instruments increases the risk of causing harm to the woman's uterus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: My concern with your argument is it's not just the anatomical line. The statute, I guess the Solicitor General referred to this as the multiple mens rea requirement. It's not simply the extraction to a particular anatomical landmark but with the purpose of demise at that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: No, but the dilation protocol certainly would be relevant on the question of intent which this statute does refer to, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: For such a doctor, a doctor who thinks that I'm trying to remove in this emergency situation as much of the fetus as possible as quickly as possible, would such a doctor often, never, sometimes be thinking what I think is likely to happen here, I'll"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: From the point of view of the doctor it would be the safest thing to avoid criminal responsibility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e533738a0fde24ae7a62184c73a5b1db3dc57872a1d1e121da35e466acf78237",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e533738a0fde-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, the answer that the Solicitor gave -- General gave to that was, you could have a pre-enforcement proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1382",
      "confidence": 0.0,
